OL,3,GNEWSA'My sex offender ex is fighting
OL,4,Afor access to our child'
OL,5,
OL,6,FA woman who is fighting to stop her sex
OL,7,Foffender ex-husband having contact with
OL,8,Ftheir child has said the thought of it
OL,9,Fmakes her "feel sick".
OL,11,FLucy - not her real name - described
OL,12,Fhow her "world was blown apart" when
OL,13,Fher then husband was convicted of
OL,14,Fpossessing indecent images of children,
OL,15,Fincluding videos of children being
OL,16,Fsexually abused.
OL,18,FShe told BBC News NI she was further
OL,19,F"horrified" to discover he was taking
OL,20,Fher to family court for supervised
OL,21,Faccess to their child.
OL,23,APub: 15-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NI NewsC Reg TVF On This Day
